SUMMARY:The Sentence and book exchange
DESCRIPTION:Petaluma Book (And Brew) Club\nPlease bring 5 books you’d li
 ke to exchange. Any books you do not want returned may be left with us\, a
 nd we will donate them to the Friends of the Library book sale.\n\nThe Sen
 tence is a 2021 novel by Louise Erdrich\, a ghost story set in a Minneapol
 is bookstore from November 2019 to November 2020\, during the pandemic and
  George Floyd protests. It follows Tookie\, a Native American woman recent
 ly released from prison\, who is haunted by the ghost of an annoying custo
 mer\, Flora\, and must unravel the mystery while navigating personal chall
 enges and a year of national turmoil. The book explores themes of grief\, 
 racism\, addiction\, and family\, blending humor with profound reflection 
 on what is owed to the living and the dead.
